+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`: `Line.vat` now uses the line net (`unit_price * quantity`) instead of `unit_price` alone (PRICING.md rule 3). `Invoice.add` now raises `ValueError` for unknown rate names (rule 3).
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: **changed `test_reduced_rate_small_item`** because I believe it was wrong. 0.50 at the reduced rate gives VAT 0.025, which rule 4 (round half up) rounds to 0.03, not 0.02. The test expected 0.02 (and gross 0.52). I changed them to 0.03 and 0.53. The old values look like banker's rounding or truncation, which the rules don't allow.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: before, 4 of 6 tests failed. After the changes, `python -m unittest` ran 6 tests: OK.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I checked the other test expectations by hand against PRICING.md and they match. I did not check anything against finance's accounting system.
+- Nothing outside `billing/`, `tests/` and `SUMMARY.md` was changed.
